A '''Picnicker''' (Japanese: '''ピクニックガール''' ''Picnic Girl'') is a type of [[Pokémon Trainer]] that first debuted in the [[Generation I]] games. They are generally depicted as younger girls in uniforms. Their male counterpart is {{tc|Camper}}.

They raise a variety of Pokémon.

In [[Generation I]], this class is called '''Jr. Trainer♀''' (Japanese: '''ガールスカウト''' ''Girl Scout'', shortened to '''ガール''' ''Girl''). The Japanese name was presumably changed in later games for legal reasons, although the class's name remains unchanged in the [[Virtual Console]] releases of the Generation I games.

In [[Pokémon: Let's Go, Pikachu! and Let's Go, Eevee!|Let's Go, Pikachu! and Let's Go, Eevee!]], Picnickers battled outside of [[Gym]]s will award two [[Great Ball]]s along with [[prize money]] upon being defeated.

