==In the TCG==
[[File:PicnickerSVPPromo114.jpg|200px|thumb|Picnicker in the TCG]]
{{main|Picnicker (SVP Promo 114)}}
'''Picnicker''' was introduced as a {{TCG|Supporter card}} in the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] during the English Scarlet & Violet Series (the Japanese Scarlet & Violet Era). It was first released in all four decks of the Japanese {{TCG|Pokémon Card Game Battle Academy}} Deck Kit. In English, it is included as a {{TCG|SVP Black Star Promos|SVP Black Star Promotional card}} included in products such as the {{TCG|Twilight Masquerade Build & Battle Box}} and the {{TCG|Battle Academy 2024}} Deck Kits. This card has the player flip a coin and draw 4 cards from their deck if it comes up heads, or 2 cards if it comes up tails.
{{left clear}}

==Trivia==
* In [[Pokémon GO]], "Picnicker" is the name of an achievement {{GO|medal}} awarded for using [[Lure Module]]s to help other Trainers catch at least five Pokémon.

